# SHA-256 of current source bytes this package compiles, installs, reads as an
# oracle, or publishes terms for, plus the independent fixture oracles it
# compares against: s2geometry v0.14.0 (tag v0.14.0, commit
# c24b368c67d0b8a2a109c5a75224e73a856bd8b7,
# https://github.com/google/s2geometry.git) and the Abseil LTS 20250814.1 tree
# vendored whole at vendor/abseil-cpp (commit
# d38452e1ee03523a208362186fd42248ff2609f6,
# https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp.git).
# One s2geometry file and seven Abseil files differ from the pinned upstream
# bytes, each a bounded portability correction, and each record keeps the
# pristine digest beside the current digest.  Exactly that 1 + 7 set, with no
# extra and no missing path, was observed by a whole-tree comparison against
# freshly pinned canonical trees,
# local://foundation-portability-canonical-source-provenance.json, not a
# pristine pass.  The earlier zero-difference vendor comparison and the
# earlier four-file comparison are history and are named as history wherever
# they are cited.
#
# 927 records, in this exact path set, grouped below:
#
#    108  A  s2geometry library translation units
#           the add_library(s2 ...) block of CMakeLists.txt, in upstream's order
#           and spelling, which is verbatim the list in
#           build_support/s2_sources.zig.  Nothing else in src/ is compiled.
#    177  B  s2geometry headers, public and internal
#           every src/s2/**.h.  Upstream installs only a hand-maintained subset
#           of these; this package installs the whole tree, so the whole tree is
#           what a consumer's #include resolves against.
#    153  C  Abseil library translation units
#           every absl_cc_library SRCS entry in the vendored tree except the
#           fourteen TESTONLY/GoogleTest-dependent ones, which is verbatim the
#           list in build_support/absl_sources.zig.
#    382  D  Abseil headers and implementation fragments
#           every vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/**.h and **.inc.  The .inc files are not
#           optional: Abseil headers #include their implementation fragments by
#           name (spinlock_linux.inc, stacktrace_x86-inl.inc, symbolize_elf.inc,
#           spinlock_win32.inc), so a header tree without them cannot compile.
#     24  E  licence, notice and dependency/build records of both upstreams
#           s2geometry LICENSE, NOTICE, AUTHORS, CONTRIBUTORS, CONTRIBUTING.md,
#           README.upstream.md (upstream's README, byte-preserved under that
#           name since 2026-10-04), CMakeLists.txt, Config.cmake.in,
#           .clang-format, setup.py,
#           pyproject.toml; Abseil LICENSE, AUTHORS, README.md,
#           CONTRIBUTING.md, UPGRADES.md, FAQ.md, CMakeLists.txt, BUILD.bazel,
#           MODULE.bazel, .clang-format, PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy, create_lts.py,
#           conanfile.py.  Abseil 20250814.1 ships no NOTICE file; its AUTHORS
#           names Google Inc. and the Apache-2.0 text in LICENSE is the notice
#           that travels.  No third-party code is compiled into any of the three
#           published static archives beyond those two upstreams: there is no
#           googletest, no Google Benchmark, no OpenSSL, no boringssl and no C
#           library of our own in libabsl.a, libs2.a or libs2bridge.a, so there
#           are no further credits to give here.  One qualification, stated here
#           rather than left to be found: for the wasm32-wasi target the Zig
#           standard library is compiled into the test, smoke and consumer
#           EXECUTABLES, not into those archives.  It is built from the pinned
#           Zig 0.16.0 compiler with the two-hunk fork patch recorded in
#           build_support/wasi_stdlib.patch, whose MIT terms travel in group J.
#     17  F  s2geometry build definitions
#           src/MODULE.bazel, src/BUILD.bazel, src/.bazelrc and the per-directory
#           src/s2/**/BUILD.bazel files.  They are upstream's definition of the
#           same source set this package enumerates, so a drift between them and
#           build_support/s2_sources.zig is a drift this record makes visible.
#     53  G  Abseil build definitions
#           every absl/**/CMakeLists.txt, every absl/**/BUILD.bazel and every
#           file under absl/copts/.  These are the SRCS blocks and the copts
#           tables this package transcribed; build_support/absl_sources.zig
#           names the target each entry came from for exactly this reason.
#      6  H  the upstream oracle files the fixtures were transcribed from
#           src/s2/s2cell_id_test.cc, s2latlng_test.cc, s2latlng_rect_test.cc,
#           s2loop_measures_test.cc, s2region_coverer_test.cc and
#           src/python/s2geometry_test.py.  Every line reference in
#           testdata/*, tests.zig, smoke.zig and zig/bridge.h resolves into one
#           of these, so a silent edit to an oracle would move the expected
#           answer instead of failing.
#      6  I  this fork's independent fixture oracles
#           testdata/*.tsv and testdata/*.txt.  NOT upstream's bytes: these are
#           this fork's transcriptions of answers published by google/s2geometry
#           and by the independent golang/geo implementation, each row carrying
#           its source file and line.  They are hashed for the same reason as the
#           rest of the set: they are the values the tests compare against, so
#           an edit to one of them would move the oracle rather than break a
#           build.
#      1  J  the pinned compiler's own licence text, carried verbatim
#           build_support/zig-0.16-LICENSE.txt, a byte-for-byte copy of the
#           LICENSE beside the pinned Zig 0.16.0 compiler
#           (5c537d6853e005298a285d508cff9ac7192cea23576c840d485b2b586a7ff177),
#           MIT Expat, "Copyright (c) Zig contributors", 21 lines.  It is here
#           because build_support/wasi_stdlib.patch modifies two upstream Zig
#           standard-library sources, and MIT requires the licence text to
#           travel with the sources it covers.  It is a licence record and
#           nothing else: it is not compiled, not installed, not read by any
#           gate, and it is not an upstream of this package.
#
# Deliberately absent, each for a stated reason:
#   zig/bridge.h, zig/bridge.cc, zig/root.zig
#                     this fork's own C bridge and Zig facade.  They are
#                     rewritten, not upstream bytes; hashing them would pin a
#                     mutable file and make an ordinary edit look like a supply
#                     change.  Their compiled source and the headers they parse
#                     are all covered above.
#   tests.zig, smoke.zig, consumer/
#                     this fork's own behavioural roots, example and standalone
#                     consumer package.  Mutable, and not an input to the library
#                     the way the oracles in group I are.
#   build.zig, build.zig.zon, build_support/
#                     this fork's own build definition.  The two source lists it
#                     carries are covered by their contents in groups A and C.
#                     build_support/ is absent with one exception, stated here
#                     rather than left to be discovered: the Zig licence copy in
#                     group J IS recorded, because it is a third-party licence
#                     text travelling for MIT's sake and not a mutable build
#                     input of this fork.  Its siblings are absent:
#                     build_support/wasi_stdlib.patch and
#                     build_support/wasi_provider.zig are fork-authored and
#                     mutable, and hashing the patched standard-library tree
#                     they produce would pin SDK-internal bytes inside a record
#                     about pinned upstreams.
#   .github/workflows/verify.yml, .gitignore
#                     this fork's CI and ignore rules; the inherited upstream
#                     .github/workflows/build.yml was removed (see FORK-NOTES.md)
#                     and is not part of any upstream tree this package carries.
#   UPSTREAM.md, NOTICE.md, CHANGELOG.md, FORK-NOTES.md, FORK-LICENSE.md,
#   README.zig.md, README.md, package.nix, flake.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml,
#   .envrc
#                     this fork's own records, its licence grant and its
#                     packaging files, listed in NOTICE.md.  README.md has been
#                     in this list rather than in group E since 2026-10-04: the
#                     fork README replaced upstream's README at that path, and
#                     upstream's bytes are preserved at README.upstream.md,
#                     which group E records under that name with the same
#                     digest and the same bytes.
#   UPSTREAM.sha256   a record cannot contain its own digest.
#   doc/, .clang-tidy, the remaining src/s2/*_test.cc,
#   src/s2/testing/*, src/python/*.cc
#                     upstream bytes that this package neither compiles, nor
#                     installs, nor reads as an oracle.  They travel in the tree
#                     for provenance and so that upstream's own CMake and Bazel
#                     builds still work; nothing here reads them.  The six files
#                     in group H are the exception, and they are listed there.
#   vendor/abseil-cpp/ci, .github, .gitignore, CMake/
#                     Abseil's own CI and packaging scaffolding.  Not compiled,
#                     not installed, not read.
#   vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/**/*_test.cc, **/*_benchmark.cc, absl/testing/**
#   vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/time/internal/cctz/testdata/**
#                     Abseil tests, benchmarks, test helpers and timezone
#                     fixtures. Retained, not compiled/installed/read by this SDK.
#
# Method: raw fs.readFileSync bytes and SHA-256 from node:crypto in Bun eval.
# The original 926 records were derived on 2026-10-01. The four modified
# Abseil files were re-derived on 2026-10-02 after their bounded portability
# patches and prominent change notices; the path set remained 926 records.
#
# One record was RENAMED on 2026-10-04: README.md is now README.upstream.md,
# with the same digest and the same bytes.  The fork README replaced upstream's
# README at that path, so the record moved to the path that still holds those
# bytes.  No digest changed and no record was added or removed, so the path set
# is still 927 records.  The fork's own new files — README.md, FORK-LICENSE.md,
# package.nix, flake.nix, devenv.nix, devenv.yaml and .envrc — are excluded
# above, on the same rule that excludes this fork's other mutable records and
# build files.
#
# On 2026-10-02 the delta grew from four Abseil files to eight, one of them in
# src/, and this record changed with it:
#   * four records now carry the current digest of an already-listed path,
#     src/s2/util/math/exactfloat/bignum.cc,
#     vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/base/internal/low_level_alloc.cc and .h, and
#     vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/time/internal/cctz/src/time_zone_format.cc.
#     Each keeps its pristine digest in the comment above it.  Those current
#     digests are the ones recorded by the whole-tree comparison
#     local://foundation-portability-canonical-source-provenance.json, which
#     hashed the file bytes on both sides of the comparison; they were not
#     re-derived by a second method here, and no claim is made that they were.
#   * one record was ADDED, build_support/zig-0.16-LICENSE.txt in group J, so
#     the path set is 927 records and not 926.  See that group for why a
#     licence text in build_support/ is recorded while the rest of that
#     directory is not.
# Every other record is byte-for-byte unchanged from the 926-record set: no
# other path was added, removed or re-derived, and every previously recorded
# pristine digest is still present beside its current one.
#
# A full `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256` replay over all 927 records has not
# been run against this revision, so no result is claimed for it; that gate is
# the parent's.  Current source/fetched replay status lives outside this
# package:
# FORKS.json.cross_test_wave.materialized_packages.s2geometry and
# local://foundation-cross-test-package-regression.json.
#
# What this record establishes: if it validates, the bytes a build compiles, the
# headers it installs and translates, the licences a redistributor must
# reproduce, the build definitions this package enumerated its sources from and
# the oracle bytes the tests compare against are the bytes pinned here, and any
# later edit to one of them fails the check loudly.
#
# What it does not establish: it is not a signature, not a Git object id, and
# not a re-derivation from either commit.  It is a hash of this working tree.
# That this tree differs from commit c24b368c67d0b8a2a109c5a75224e73a856bd8b7
# in exactly one disclosed path, and that the vendored Abseil differs from
# d38452e1ee03523a208362186fd42248ff2609f6 in exactly seven, rests on the
# import, on the two `git archive` digests recorded in UPSTREAM.md, and on the
# CI step that extracts both canonical archives at those digests and compares
# the whole trees path by path against the eight pairs of digests carried
# here.  There is deliberately no `git diff --exit-code <commit> -- src` step in
# CI: a zero-diff check cannot express "exactly these paths", so it would
# either pass only while nothing at all is modified, or fail on the very file a
# disclosed fix is about.  The Abseil revision rests on the tag/commit pair, on
# the CI check that reads `lts_20250814` out of
# vendor/abseil-cpp/absl/base/options.h, and on this file: the driver's
# source-archive set
# (local://foundation-expansion-source-archives.json) records a `git archive`
# digest for the eight top-level projects and has no entry for the nested Abseil
# dependency, so no such digest is claimed here.
#
# Verify with:  sha256sum -c UPSTREAM.sha256
# Current source/fetched replay status is driver-owned under the package closure.

